// 05 — Is Network Protection actually firing (empirical, not configured-state)
//
// Purpose      04 says what is configured. This says what is happening. Configuration
//              assessment can report compliant while the component emits nothing —
//              policy applied is not the same as policy enforced.
// Table        DeviceEvents
// Permission   ThreatHunting.Read.All
// Expected     Non-zero ExploitGuardNetworkProtection* events across a meaningful
//              device count over 30 days. Audited-only is fine for detection purposes;
//              the C2 rule needs RemoteUrl to be populated, not blocked.
// Read it as   Zero events + compliant config in 04 == treat RemoteUrl as unreliable
//              and rely on the other five rules for coverage of this actor.
//
// startswith rather than an exact ActionType list: the Blocked/Audited suffix pair is
// documented, but asserting exact names risks a false zero if the vocabulary differs.

DeviceEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(30d)
| where ActionType startswith "ExploitGuardNetworkProtection"
| summarize Events   = count(),
            Devices  = dcount(DeviceId),
            FirstSeen = min(Timestamp),
            LastSeen  = max(Timestamp)
    by ActionType
| order by Events desc
| limit 50
